CHANGELOG.md:162:- **T2.H2 — Neural U-Net denoiser revival** (`@vitrum/walkaround-hybrid` + `@vitrum/core`): Rebuilds the neural denoiser from scratch, fixing all 8 correctness blockers from the Sprint 13 scaffold that was deleted during the sweep-2026-05-11 review. The `'neural'` denoiser mode is **opt-in** — default remains `'atrous-variance'`. No trained weights are shipped; users collect a dataset and run `tools/neural-denoiser-training/train.py`. The 8 bugs fixed vs. the prior scaffold: **(1) Skip-connection spatial mismatch** — `unetArchitecture.ts` now uses pre-downsampling encoder feature maps (enc1_feat, enc2_feat, enc3_feat) as skip sources, ensuring every skipAdd layer's operands have matching (H, W, C); tests verify this analytically at 64×64 and 128×64. **(2) `enc_input` never assembled** — `inputPacker.ts` (new file) provides a GPU compute shader that packs noisyColor + albedo + normals (3+3+3 channels) into a per-pixel interleaved H×W×9 buffer; `InferenceGraph` calls this packing pass before dispatching the graph. **(3) Binding index mismatch** — All 5 WGSL kernels (`conv2d`, `transposedConv2d`, `relu`, `skipConnection`, `bilinearUpsample`) declare the canonical binding order input=0, weights/inputB=1, biases=2, output=3, params=4; the host dispatch in `InferenceGraph._buildBindGroup` uses the same order; Test 2 parses `@binding()` declarations from WGSL source and asserts consistency. **(4) Uniform buffer never written** — `InferenceGraph.initialize()` calls `device.queue.writeBuffer()` with the actual shape params (`inputH`, `inputW`, `inC`, `outC`, `kH`, `kW`, `stride`, `padding`) immediately after allocation, AND re-writes per layer on each `run()` call; `_uniformWriteCount` counter is exposed for test instrumentation; Test 3 verifies the counter and the packed param layout. **(5) `train.py.md` not executable** — `tools/neural-denoiser-training/train.py` is a real Python file with a `UNetDenoiser` (PyTorch) matching the architecture, L1+SSIM composite loss (Chaitanya 2017), Adam + cosine LR schedule, and exports `weights.bin` at training end; `python -m py_compile` verified. **(6) Bind-group cache not stable** — `InferenceGraph.run()` tracks buffer identity via `cachedBufKeys` and rebuilds the bind group if any buffer changes (e.g. after a resize via re-`initialize()`). **(7) `dispose()` doesn't clear slot-by-slot** — `dispose()` nulls each `cachedBindGroup` slot individually via a for-loop, then reassigns `_layerStates = new Array(N).fill(null)` so GPUBindGroup references release before the underlying buffers are destroyed. **(8) No `'neural'` mode in `HybridEngine`** — `HybridEngineOptions.denoiser` union extends to include `'neural'`; `HybridEngine` constructor validates `neuralWeights` is provided (throws with a helpful error pointing to `tools/neural-denoiser-training/README.md`); `HybridEngine._initPipeline` creates and initializes the `InferenceGraph` before pipeline init; `WalkaroundGPUPipeline.initialize` stores the graph and dispatches it in `renderFrame` when `_denoiserMode === 'neural'`. New binary format: `.vitrum-model` (header: `u32 magic=0xDEAF1984`, `u32 version=1`, `u32 layerCount`; per-layer: nameLen+name+weightCount+weights+biasCount+biases); weight layout OIKW for Conv2D, IOKW for ConvTranspose2D matching PyTorch defaults. `tools/neural-denoiser-training/export_weights.py` (new, standalone): converts any `.pth` checkpoint to the vitrum binary without running train.py. `@vitrum/core` `EngineOptions.denoiser` union extended with `'neural'`. 21 tests in `__tests__/neural.test.ts` across 5 groups. References: Ronneberger et al. 2015 (U-Net, MICCAI, https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.04597); Chaitanya et al. 2017 (RDA, SIGGRAPH, https://doi.org/10.1145/3072959.3073601).
