CHANGELOG.md:310:- **`HybridEngine.setSize()` for cheap canvas resize** (`@vitrum/walkaround-hybrid`, d4fb73b): pre-fix, `HybridEngine` had no `setSize` API — hosts had to recreate the entire engine on every canvas resize or DPR change. React's `ResizeObserver` storms compounded this: each tick churned the BVH (50–500 ms CPU build), every compiled pipeline shader (50–500 ms), every DDGI atlas, and ~1 GB of `FrameResources` textures. Fix: new `WalkaroundGPUPipeline.resize(W, H)` destroys and recreates only the per-frame `FrameResources` (full-res rgba16float textures, reservoir buffers, variance buffers, GTAO half/full, SVGF persistent textures), resets ping-pong indices + frame counters, and preserves BVH buffers, all compiled compute pipelines, bind-group layouts, DDGI atlases, per-pass UBOs, timestamp state. Bind groups are rebuilt per-frame in `renderFrame()` so the resize automatically picks up next frame. New `HybridEngine.setSize(W, H)` updates `_width / _height` and delegates to `_pipeline.resize()` when live; defensively no-ops on identical / zero / negative sizes and pre-init pipeline. Cost: 5–30 ms on a 4K surface vs 500–2000 ms for full teardown + re-init. DDGI atlas survives unchanged (world-space, not screen-space). NOT added to the core `Engine` interface — `pt-webgl` resizes internally via `FrameInput.viewport.{width,height}`; each backend manages its own resize semantics. 9 tests in `__tests__/hybridEngineSetSize.test.ts`.
CHANGELOG.md:314:- **In-flight init guard prevents concurrent setScene leaks** (`@vitrum/walkaround-hybrid`, 01bf92e): `HybridEngine._initPipeline()` was fire-and-forget with no in-flight guard. When the host (or vitrum's own factory bootstrap) called `setScene()` while a previous `_initPipeline()` was still running, both async chains wrote to shared state (`_bvhBuffers`, `_pipeline`, `_ddgiTraversalScene`) at multiple points after several `await` boundaries — last writer won; the loser leaked ~1 GB of GPU resources (18 rgba16float full-res textures + BVH buffers + DDGI atlases). React StrictMode + window resize storms compounded this. Fix: every `_initPipeline()` captures a monotonic `mySeq = ++this._initSeq` at entry; before each shared-state write the chain re-checks `mySeq === this._initSeq`. On mismatch it disposes its locals (BVH + synthesized THREE root + pipeline) in a `finally` block and bails without mutating shared state. Two checkpoints cover the two await boundaries (`buildReSTIRSceneBVH` and `pipeline.initialize()`). Adds `_pendingTeardown` flag so `dispose()` (above) can keep its synchronous contract. 5 new tests in `__tests__/hybridEngineInitRace.test.ts`.
