HARDWARE-VALIDATION-NEEDS.md:201:- **What changed:** PPG was train-only (learned a dTree but gi-ris sampled plain cosine; the guide output had no reader). gi-ris now draws GI candidate directions from the learned dTree with a defensive, UNBIASED MIS mixture: with prob α from the dTree else cosine, and the RIS source pdf is `α·p_guide + (1−α)·p_cos` evaluated for the chosen direction. New `ppg/ppgPdf.wgsl.ts` (`ppgEvalPdf` mirrors CPU `dTreePdf`); the 3 PPG buffers packed into the hybridLayers bind group (group 3, bindings 6/7/8, respecting maxBindGroups=4); `ppgEnabled`/`ppgMixAlpha` UBO gate. ppg-OFF (α=0) is bit-identical to the pre-PPG cosine kernel (no extra RNG draw; literal `w = luminance(Lo)`).
HARDWARE-VALIDATION-NEEDS.md:228:- **Storage-buffer budget (confirm, do not assume):** the spatial/temporal GI pipelines now bind the shared scene group, so they reference at most 2 reservoir buffers (group 0) + the scene BVH subset they traverse — **fewer scene buffers than the already-shipping `shade`/`ris` pipelines** (which declare the full 11-entry scene group and work on the full tier). In merged-BVH mode the visibility ray touches only the 3 BVH buffers (nodes/index/position); TLAS slots are declared-but-untraversed (same discipline as shade). Confirm pipeline creation succeeds on the full tier; lite tier forbids the heavy GI features anyway but the GI reuse passes themselves stay within budget. **No budget overflow was introduced** — but verify on a real device.
HARDWARE-VALIDATION-NEEDS.md:238:- **HONEST BIAS CAVEAT (read first):** NRC is a **BIASED cache** — the MLP prediction *replaces* the true path suffix at the spread-termination vertex; it is a *learned approximation*, NOT an unbiased Monte-Carlo estimate. Unlike V18 (BDPT MIS) / V19 (GRIS) which preserve the converged MEAN, NRC does **NOT** — its value is variance reduction / faster convergence / lower noise with **bounded bias**. The acceptance is *perceptual closeness to the no-NRC reference within tolerance, with measurably faster convergence / lower noise*, **NOT** "equal converged mean." Do not assert mean-equality for NRC. NRC is opt-in / full-tier only — **it cannot run on lite / SwiftShader** (hash-grid feature tables + fused-MLP weight/Adam buffers exceed the lite budget; the ctor throws on `tier:'lite' + nrcEnabled`).
HARDWARE-VALIDATION-NEEDS.md:240:  1. **LIVE cache QUERY at the gi-ris suffix vertex.** `buildRisGiNrcModule` (`shaders/risGiNrc.wgsl.ts`) is the NRC variant of the Sprint-16 gi-ris pass. At the reconnection vertex `xs`, it tracks Müller's path spread (§5) along the bounce edge; when `a(x) > c·a₀` fires it REPLACES the DDGI suffix estimate (`Lo = irrAtXs·albedo·INV_PI`) with the MLP's predicted outgoing radiance — an INLINE single-sample MLP forward (`wgsl/nrcQuery.wgsl.ts` `nrcMlpForward`, reading the trainer's f32 master weight/bias buffers + the hash-grid tables, running the multiresolution-hash-grid + one-blob + raw-feature encode INLINE since WGSL forbids storage-pointer function args). Below the spread threshold it keeps the DDGI estimate verbatim (sub-threshold regions are bit-identical to the OFF pass).
